: Episode 1 - Transportation</title><link>https://www.selenium.dev/blog/2020/how-selenium-works-transport/</link><pubDate>Wed, 10 Jun 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.selenium.dev/blog/2020/how-selenium-works-transport/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;After an interaction on the last weekend of January 2020, on a Selenium Issue where someone said “why can’t you just…” after I explained the issue I thought that I would start explaining commands in Selenium WebDriver and why we landed on the design that we have today.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I will repeat this on every page of the series but a lot, an annoying amount sometimes, of thinking goes into how every little bit of Selenium works.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Public Project Meeting - June 04, 2020</title><link>https://www.selenium.dev/blog/2020/public-project-meeting-20200604/</link><pubDate>Thu, 04 Jun 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.selenium.dev/blog/2020/public-project-meeting-20200604/</guid><description>&lt;div class="row justify-content-center my-1"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="alert alert-blue col-10 alert-dismissible fade show mb-0 -bg-selenium-yellow" role="alert"&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;h4 class="alert-heading pb-2 text-center"&gt;Archived meeting minutes&lt;/h4&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;div class="w-100 text-center"&gt;&#10; All meeting minutes can now be found &lt;a href="https://www.selenium.dev/meetings/"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;button type="button" class="close" data-bs-dismiss="alert" aria-label="Close"&gt;&#10; &lt;span aria-hidden="true"&gt;&amp;times;&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Continuing the series of bi-weekly public project meetings, here is the&#10;timeline of the meeting held on June 04, 2020 (times are on IST).&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Meetings are held on the &lt;code&gt;#selenium-tlc&lt;/code&gt; channel on &lt;a href="https://seleniumhq.slack.com/join/shared_invite/enQtODAwOTUzOTM5OT